<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A brief, dismissible notification that stacks in a corner of the screen.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/toast)

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :default %>

## Usage

Render one `Toaster` near the end of your layout's `<body>` - the viewport every toast appears in:

```ruby
# app/views/layouts/application.rb (a Phlex layout) - or `<%%= render UI::Toaster.new %>` in ERB
body do
  yield
  Toaster(toasts: flash_toasts)
end
```

Then fire toasts from wherever it's convenient:

```ruby
# From the server: flash messages rendered with the page…
def flash_toasts
  flash.map { |type, message| { title: message, icon: type == "alert" ? :error : :success } }
end

# …or appended from a controller action / broadcast with Turbo Streams
turbo_stream.append "toaster", UI::Toast.new(title: "Changes saved", icon: :success)

# From a button, without writing JavaScript
ToastTrigger(toast: { title: "Changes saved" }) { |trigger| Button(**trigger) { "Save" } }
```

```js
// From JavaScript - Appica's useToastManager()
import { toast } from "ui/toast/toast"   // also available as window.UI.toast

toast.add({ title: "Changes saved", description: "Your preferences have been updated." })
```

A toast is data - a title, description, an optional icon, an action button - and the Toaster renders,
stacks, and animates it. Each one auto-dismisses after its timeout (5s by default, paused while you hover
the stack), can be swiped away toward its edge, and has a close button. Hover or focus the stack to expand it.

## Examples

### With an icon

`icon:` adds a filled, color-matched glyph - `:success`, `:error`, `:warning`, `:info`, `:bell` or `:loading`
(a spinner) - while the surface stays neutral.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :icons %>

### With a thumbnail

`thumbnail: true` wraps the icon in a tinted badge for more prominence.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :thumbnails %>

### With an action

`action:` renders an inline button - an "Undo", "Retry", or "View". On the server give it an `href:`, an
`event:` name (dispatched on `window` with `{ toast: id }`) or a follow-up `toast:`; from JavaScript an
`onClick` function.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :action %>

```ruby
Toast(title: "Message archived", action: { label: "Undo", href: unarchive_message_path(message) })
```

```js
toast.add({ title: "Message archived", action: { label: "Undo", onClick: () => restore(id) } })
```

### Promise

`toast.promise(promise, { loading, success, error })` swaps the content as the promise settles - ideal for
saves and uploads. States can be objects or functions of the value / error.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :promise %>

```js
toast.promise(fetch("/documents", { method: "POST" }), {
  loading: { title: "Saving…", icon: "loading", thumbnail: true },
  success: { title: "Saved", icon: "success", thumbnail: true },
  error: { title: "Could not save", icon: "error", thumbnail: true }
})
```

### Positions

`Toaster(position:)` anchors the stack - any of the six corners and edges. A single toast can target another
one with `position:`. Toasts swipe toward their nearest edge to dismiss.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :positions %>

### Timeout & progress

`timeout:` controls how long a toast lingers; `timeout: 0` keeps it until dismissed. `Toaster(progress: true)`
draws a thin countdown bar on auto-dismissing toasts (paused while the stack is expanded).

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :timeout %>

### Server-rendered (flash)

Toasts rendered with the page animate in and time out like any other - this is how flash messages and Turbo
Stream appends arrive.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :server_rendered %>

### RTL

The layout mirrors: the icon leads from the right, the close button moves to the left, and the progress bar
drains in the reading direction.

<%= embed UI::ToastPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Toaster

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `position:` | `:top_left`, `:top_center`, `:top_right`, `:bottom_left`, `:bottom_center`, `:bottom_right` | `:bottom_right` | Where the stack is anchored; also sets the swipe-to-dismiss directions. |
| `timeout:` | `Integer` (ms) | `5000` | Default auto-dismiss delay for toasts that don't set their own. |
| `limit:` | `Integer` | `3` | Maximum toasts shown at once; the rest wait until there's room. |
| `progress:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Countdown bar on auto-dismissing toasts. |
| `toasts:` | `Array<Hash>` | `[]` | Toasts rendered with the page (the options of `UI::Toast`). |
| `id:` | `String` | `"toaster"` | Id of the default viewport - the Turbo Stream target. |

### Toast

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `title:` | `String` | - | The toast heading. |
| `description:` | `String` | - | Supporting body text. |
| `icon:` | `:success`, `:error`, `:warning`, `:info`, `:bell`, `:loading` | - | Leading glyph (or pass a block for your own). |
| `thumbnail:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Wrap the icon in a tinted badge. |
| `action:` | `{ label:, href: / event: / toast:, variant: }` | - | Inline action button. |
| `timeout:` | `Integer` (ms) | Toaster's | Auto-dismiss delay; `0` keeps it until dismissed. |
| `priority:` | `:low`, `:high` | `:low` | `:high` interrupts screen readers (`role="alert"`) - use for errors. |
| `type:` | `String` | - | Free-form category, exposed as `data-type` for styling. |
| `dismissible:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Render the close button. |
| `close_label:` | `String` | `"Dismiss"` | Accessible label for the close button. |

### JavaScript: `toast` (`import { toast } from "ui/toast/toast"` / `window.UI.toast`)

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `add(options) → id` | Show a toast. Options mirror `UI::Toast` in camelCase, plus `position`, `onClose` and `action.onClick`. |
| `update(id, options)` | Patch a toast in place. |
| `close(id)` | Dismiss a toast. |
| `promise(promise, { loading, success, error })` | Drive a toast through loading / success / error. |

The Toaster also dispatches `ui--toaster:close` with `{ id }` when a toast is removed.

### ToastTrigger

`ToastTrigger(toast: { … })` fires a toast on click. A block taking an argument puts the attributes on your
own element: `ToastTrigger(toast: { title: "Saved" }) { |trigger| Button(**trigger) { "Save" } }`.

## Accessibility

- Each viewport is a labelled `aria-live="polite"` region, so new toasts are announced politely. Set
  `priority: :high` on important ones (errors, warnings) to announce them immediately.
- The close button carries an accessible label (`close_label:`); it's hidden from the accessibility tree until
  the stack is hovered or focused, then revealed.
- Timers pause while the stack is hovered or focused, and while the window is in the background.
- Keep toast text short and self-contained - toasts disappear, so don't put the only copy of critical
  information in one.
- Enter/exit, stacking and swipe animations honor `prefers-reduced-motion`, and the progress bar is hidden.
